---
import PrivacyLayout from "../../components/PrivacyLayout.astro";
---

<PrivacyLayout
    title="Privacy Policy - Denaro App"
    appName="Denaro"
    lastUpdated="31 agosto 2025"
    accentColor="#3498db"
>
    <div class="highlight">
        <strong>In summary:</strong> Denaro is a primarily offline finance management
        app. We do not collect your personal financial data. The app displays advertising
        through Google AdMob, which may collect some data to personalize ads according
        to their policies.
    </div>

    <div class="warning">
        <strong>Important:</strong> Denaro uses Google AdMob to display advertisements.
        AdMob may collect some data according to their own privacy policies.
    </div>

    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
        Denaro is a mobile application for personal finance management designed
        to work completely offline. The app is developed with the goal of
        ensuring maximum privacy and security of user data.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Data we do NOT collect ourselves</h2>
    <p>Denaro does not directly collect, transmit, share, or sell:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Financial information (balances, transactions, buckets)</li>
        <li>Personally identifiable information</li>
        <li>App usage information</li>
        <li>Location data</li>
        <li>Device information</li>
        <li>Biometric data or security PINs</li>
        <li>Language preferences or other settings</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Advertising and Google AdMob</h2>
    <p>To support app development, we use Google AdMob which may collect:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Advertising identifiers (Advertising ID)</li>
        <li>Device information (model, OS version)</li>
        <li>App usage data for advertising purposes</li>
        <li>Network and connection information</li>
        <li>Approximate location data (for geo-targeted ads)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        This data is handled directly by Google according to their
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank"
            >Privacy Policy</a
        >
        and
        <a
            href="https://support.google.com/admob/answer/6128543"
            target="_blank">AdMob Policies</a
        >.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Advertising controls</h2>
    <p>You can control ad personalization:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Android:</strong> Settings > Google > Ads > Opt out of Ads Personalization
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>iOS:</strong> Settings > Privacy & Security > Apple Advertising
            > Personalized Ads
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Reset Advertising ID:</strong> you can reset your advertising
            ID from device settings
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        For more information visit:
        <a href="https://support.google.com/ads/answer/2662922" target="_blank"
            >Control the ads you see</a
        >
    </p>

    <h2>5. Where your data is stored</h2>
    <p>All data you enter in Denaro is stored exclusively:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>On your local device</strong> in an encrypted SQLite database
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>In the device's secure storage</strong> for security settings
            (PIN)
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>In the app's local storage</strong> for preferences (language,
            theme)
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        We do not use cloud servers, automatic backup services, or remote
        databases for financial data.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Data security</h2>
    <p>Your data is protected through:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Database encryption:</strong> the SQLite database is encrypted
            with randomly generated keys
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Local authentication:</strong> PIN and biometric authentication
            managed exclusively by the operating system
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>App isolation:</strong> financial data is accessible only by
            the Denaro app on your device
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Limited transmission:</strong> only advertising data is transmitted
            to AdMob
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Optional security features</h2>
    <p>The app offers optional security features:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Access PIN:</strong> stored securely on the device using Expo
            SecureStore
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Biometric authentication:</strong> managed directly by the device's
            operating system
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>This security data is never transmitted or shared.</p>

    <h2>8. App permissions</h2>
    <p>Denaro only requests the minimum necessary permissions:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Local storage:</strong> to save financial data on the device
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Internet access:</strong> required to display advertisements
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Biometric authentication (optional):</strong> if you choose to
            enable this feature
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        We do not request access to contacts, camera, microphone, location, or
        other sensitive data.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Third-party services</h2>
    <p>Denaro integrates the following third-party services:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Google AdMob:</strong> for advertising (subject to Google policies)
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        We do not use other analytics or tracking services beyond those
        necessary for advertising.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Backup and synchronization</h2>
    <p>
        Denaro does not offer cloud backup or automatic synchronization
        features. You are responsible for backing up your data through:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Device backup (if supported by the operating system)</li>
        <li>Future export tools we may add</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>11. User rights</h2>
    <p>
        Since we do not collect personal data, you always have complete control:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Access:</strong> all your data is visible in the app
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Modification:</strong> you can edit or delete any data directly
            in the app
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Deletion:</strong> uninstalling the app removes all associated
            data
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Portability:</strong> your data remains on your device
        </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        For advertising data, refer to Google AdMob controls mentioned in
        section 4.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Data transfers</h2>
    <p>Advertising data may be transferred and processed:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>On Google servers (located in various countries)</li>
        <li>According to Google's data transfer regulations</li>
        <li>With protections provided by Google policies</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>13. Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>Any changes to this privacy policy will be communicated through:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>App updates in the stores</li>
        <li>In-app notifications (if implemented)</li>
        <li>Publication of the updated version</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>14. Regulatory compliance</h2>
    <p>Denaro is designed to comply with:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>GDPR (General Data Protection Regulation)</strong>
        </li>
        <li><strong>CCPA (California Consumer Privacy Act)</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Other privacy regulations</strong></li>
    </ul>
    <p>Google AdMob has its own regulatory compliance certifications.</p>

    <div class="highlight">
        <strong>Remember:</strong> Your financial data never leaves your device.
        Only advertising data is handled by Google AdMob according to their policies.
    </div>

    <div slot="additional-contact">
        <p>
            For advertising-related matters, contact
            <a
                href="https://support.google.com/ads/contact/abg_afc"
                target="_blank">Google AdMob Support</a
            >
            directly.
        </p>
    </div>
</PrivacyLayout>
